audisp-syslog: include <unistd.h> for getppid()

audisp-syslog.c calls getppid() in its SIGTERM handler but never includes
<unistd.h>. On glibc the prototype leaks in through some other header
audit-userspace pulls in and the build stays quiet; musl does not leak
it, so the build fails with

  audisp-syslog.c: In function 'term_handler':
  audisp-syslog.c:54:37: error: implicit declaration of function 'getppid'

Every sibling audisp plugin (statsd, remote, ids, filter, af_unix,
zos-remote) already includes <unistd.h> for the same reason. Match them.

Submitted upstream as https://github.com/linux-audit/audit-userspace/pull/551.
Drop this patch once the fix lands in a tagged release.

--- a/audisp/plugins/syslog/audisp-syslog.c
+++ b/audisp/plugins/syslog/audisp-syslog.c
@@ -28,6 +28,7 @@
 #include <sys/select.h>
 #include <errno.h>
 #include <syslog.h>
+#include <unistd.h>
 #include <stdlib.h>
 #ifdef HAVE_LIBCAP_NG
 #include <cap-ng.h>
